CrowdStrike Query Language catalogs (data/catalogs/cql/), generated by
scripts/engine/sync_cql_catalog.py. They hold facts (names, types, parameters,
values, platforms) and descriptions written for this repository. No prose,
code or query of any source below is copied into them. The commit or date of
each source is in the header of each TOML file.

functions.toml
  Function names, parameters, parameter types, defaults, enumerated values,
  bounds, categories, contexts and versions from the CrowdStrike Query
  Language function reference, https://library.humio.com/crowdstrike-query-language/
  (Copyright CrowdStrike, Inc., all rights reserved), and the removals in its
  release notes. Facts only; `docs` and `deprecated_note` are written here.
  `ngsiem` cites CrowdStrike/logscale-community-content (below).

events.toml and fields.toml
  - CrowdStrike/logscale-community-content: released into the public domain
    under the Unlicense (LICENSE-Unlicense.txt). Its sub-packages
    Log-Sources/CrowdStrike/FLTR/crowdstrike-fltrcore and crowdstrike-fltrlolbins
    are MIT License, Copyright (c) 2023 CrowdStrike (LICENSE-MIT.txt), listed
    as source `lcc-mit`; the Log-Sources packages Airlock, Microsoft
    Security-Overview, Imperva CloudWAF, Cisco ASA, Cisco Meraki-Systems-Manager,
    Palo-Alto PAN-Firewall-Parser-Only, Google ChromeEnterpriseSecurity and
    00-Vendor-Template are Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt), listed
    as source `lcc-apache`. Event, field, tag and value names seen in its
    queries.
  - ByteRay-Labs/Query-Hub: MIT License, as its readme states
    (LICENSE-MIT.txt). Event and field names seen in its queries (`queryhub`).
  - cs-shadowbq/CQL-Queries: MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 cs-shadowbq
    (LICENSE-MIT.txt). Event, field and tag names seen in its queries
    (`cqlqueries`).
  - Azure/Azure-Sentinel, Solutions/CrowdStrike Falcon Endpoint Protection:
    MIT License, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation (LICENSE-MIT.txt). The
    event to table routing of the FDR connector and each table's column names
    (`sentinel`, `categories`).
  - SigmaHQ/pySigma-backend-crowdstrike, sigma/pipelines/crowdstrike/crowdstrike.py:
    GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1. Only the event names and the target
    field names of its CrowdStrike Falcon pipeline are used, as facts; no code
    is copied or linked (`pysigma`).
  - Elastic Common Schema (elastic/ecs), through data/catalogs/ecs/fields.json:
    Copyright Elasticsearch B.V., Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE-Apache-2.0.txt,
    data/catalogs/ecs/NOTICE). Names and types of the ECS fields the CPS layer
    lists (`ecs`).
  - Built-in field and tag names and the CrowdStrike Parsing Standard tags:
    facts from library.humio.com and developer.crowdstrike.com (Copyright
    CrowdStrike, Inc.); descriptions written here.

Not used: Elastic's crowdstrike integration (Elastic License 2.0), so no name
only it supplies is listed; and any copy of CrowdStrike's login-gated events
data dictionary.
